			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852779">
									

<p>Seeking Greenlights: No</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Drama</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): Interview Logs, Incident Reports</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: A young orphan boy is found in possession of a quilt that creates a play-world which he can escape to as a place of refuge.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: Local reports of a small town indicate that a young boy has been missing for a few weeks after his grandmother passed away. Photographs inside the house reveal nothing out of the ordinary, except for a quilt with thaumaturgical symbols.</p>
<p>A team is sent to the house, whereupon they discover a diary written by the boy's grandmother, detailing that she knitted the quilt, which creates a play-world that the boy can inhabit. She mentions that the quilt's world can be entered with a password, and that she suspects the boy will retreat there upon her passing.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If no one is inhabiting the quilt's play world, its anomalous properties are rendered inert, so SCP decides to attempt to retrieve the boy. First, a D-class is sent into the world as a scout. He discovers a fantasy land divided into four distinct sections. In the center of the world is a large castle surrounded by a city. The world itself is quite safe, with food readily available and the artificial denizens being rather helpful. Each section is guarded by a powerful creature, and upon annoying the boy - who is near-omniscient in the world - he is &quot;killed&quot; by a guardian and expelled from the quilt's world, though he is unharmed when he emerges.</p>
<p>An MTF team is sent in next, which intrigues the boy, as he's never met soldiers before. He encourages the team to play a game with him, wherein they are sent on a quest to kill the dragon of the desert section. As outside weapons are rendered inoperable in the world, they retrieve &quot;magical weapons&quot; that work in the world and slay the dragon, advancing to the castle town. However, they anger the boy upon mentioning his grandmother, and are &quot;slain&quot; by the townsfolk.</p>
<p>The final person to enter the world is a pediatric therapist, who arrives on an almost uninhabited mountain. She dodges the guardian over the next few days, developing a rapport with the boy as he watches her, and secures an audience, where she helps him through his grief. The boy exits the world, SCP secures the quilt, and amnestics are applied. Later, the boy is given a replica of his grandmother's quilt, without anomalous properties.</p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: The main draw of the story is the whimsy and fantastical nature of the world, contrasted with the boy's mental state. The world reacts to his emotions. It also shows that the Foundation is cold, but not inhuman, and the gentle route in this case is the path of least resistance.</p>
<p>Additional Notes:</p>
